                <pb facs="0463" n="1197" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1197"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Spanish minister
                    and has the honor to acknowledge, with thanks, the receipt of the minister’s
                    note of the 1st instant, with which is inclosed an account of the sitting held
                    by the Spanish Senate on the 15th ultimo, at which sitting the Government was
                    questioned by Señor Ortiz de Pinedo, senator for the Island of Cuba, as to the
                    observance by the United States of its neutrality laws.</p>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State has read with pleasure the deserved tribute paid by
                    the Duke of Tetuan to the impartial friendliness of this Government.</p>
            </div>
